  "note": "The two files that used to be recorded as drift are converged: assets_route.py had CRLF line endings on the NAS against an LF repository blob, and scripts/assets_mirror.py was an older revision that fetched one object at a time. Both were replaced by the -Apply this record describes. What the deployment also had to survive is the LAN proxy: it is an Xray container that another job restarts regularly for node selection (47 config reloads on 2026-10-10, and a restart at 15:28:02Z), and a tick that loses one connection used to lose the whole six-hour round. The deployed mirror now retries a transient transport failure and fetches eight objects at a time, which is why the 419-object release above took three minutes instead of never finishing.",
